  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An electron enters a region of uniform magnetic field at a speed v. The direction of the electron is perpendicular to the magnetic field. The path of the electron inside the magnetic field is circular with radius r.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The speed of the electron is varied to obtain different values of r.</p>\n<p>Which graph represents the variation of speed v with r?</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
